  "title": "Counterweight Crossing",
  "rules": [
    "The river column can be crossed only at north and south bridge sites. Entry requires the bridge's recorded open flag.",
    "The heavier west plate opens the north bridge; the heavier east plate opens the south bridge. Equal loads close both unless braced.",
    "An agent weighs one, an evacuee one, and ballast two. Carried mass and dropped objects contribute at their actual positions.",
    "Carry at most one object. The porter moves ballast every tick; the escort moves evacuees every tick; other loaded workers move on even input ticks.",
    "Brace an adjacent bridge using one energy. The engineer holds it for three ticks, other workers for one. Waiting recovers energy.",
    "Bridge configurations update after movement, so lifting or leaving a plate changes the next tick's access. A closed span never crushes its occupant; exit remains possible.",
    "Deliver four evacuees, then each empty worker may evacuate at shelter. An evacuated worker cannot return to maintain a plate."
  ],
